1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,486
Why isn't this a Spring bean?

2
00:00:01,606 --> 00:00:03,120
A class on the classpath

3
00:00:03,120 --> 00:00:06,060
isn't automatically registered.

4
00:00:06,060 --> 00:00:08,786
Give Spring a registration path.

5
00:00:08,966 --> 00:00:09,920
Register configuration

6
00:00:09,920 --> 00:00:12,660
with a @Bean method.

7
00:00:12,660 --> 00:00:14,020
Spring calls the factory

8
00:00:14,020 --> 00:00:16,751
and manages its result.

9
00:00:16,931 --> 00:00:19,440
Or add the @Component annotation,

10
00:00:19,440 --> 00:00:20,540
then scan the package

11
00:00:20,540 --> 00:00:22,586
containing your class.

12
00:00:22,766 --> 00:00:23,680
Miss that package,

13
00:00:23,680 --> 00:00:25,560
and even an annotated class

14
00:00:25,560 --> 00:00:27,821
stays unregistered.

15
00:00:28,001 --> 00:00:29,640
Our tests retrieve both.

16
00:00:29,640 --> 00:00:31,880
Two paths, one result:

17
00:00:31,880 --> 00:00:34,679
Spring knows which beans to manage.

18
00:00:36,679 --> 00:00:38,037
Thanks for watching.

